diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..170e4b9 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,51 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys and account security
+
+Sign up or sign in with your existing password, then open **Account security** in
+the header to add a passkey. Returning users can use the passkey button or browser
+autofill on the sign-in page. The security page supports multiple passkeys,
+names, creation and last-used dates, removal, display-name updates, and identity
+confirmation with a passkey or password. Password authentication continues to use
+the existing Times password service; no passwords are stored locally. Accounts
+are linked to local passkey records only after successful password authentication.
+
+The server uses SimpleWebAuthn to verify signatures, origin, RP ID, user presence,
+and user verification. Challenges expire after five minutes and are consumed
+once. Auth sessions expire after 24 hours, use opaque tokens in HttpOnly,
+SameSite cookies, and rotate on sign-in. Credential changes require identity
+confirmation within five minutes. Password sign-in remains available after the
+last passkey is removed. Optional WebAuthn Signal APIs synchronize password
+managers when supported; passkey nicknames are local labels.
+
+Use Node **22.13 or later** (Node 24 recommended). Configure at runtime:
+
+| Variable | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `AUTH_ORIGIN` | Exact public origin, including scheme and nonstandard port, e.g. `https://news.example.com`. Defaults to the configured Astro production site; development uses the local origin. Set `http://localhost:11224` when serving a production build locally. |
+| `AUTH_RP_ID` | Optional stable relying party domain. Defaults to the hostname of `AUTH_ORIGIN`; it must match or be a valid domain suffix of that hostname. Credentials are tied to this domain. |
+| `AUTH_DB_PATH` | SQLite database path. Defaults to `.data/auth.sqlite`. Use a persistent writable volume in deployment and back it up. |
+
+HTTPS is required outside localhost. The SQLite store supports one application
+instance with durable storage; multiple replicas require a shared transactional
+database and shared rate limits before deployment. Keep the RP ID stable across
+releases. The existing remote password service must remain available for
+password registration, password sign-in, and password confirmation.
+
+Provider names and icons are a small local snapshot of the
+ [passkey authenticator AAGUID registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids)
+(retrieved October 14, 2026). Unknown providers use a generic key icon. Provider
+metadata is only a display hint and never affects access decisions.
+
+```sh
+pnpm test            # Real cryptographic WebAuthn server flow and security tests
+pnpm run check:auth  # Type-check authentication implementation
+pnpm run build
+```
+
+The repository-wide TypeScript check currently reports existing errors in
+`MenuButton.tsx` and `utils/images.ts`; `check:auth` isolates the authentication
+implementation. Tests use a software authenticator and a stub for the remote
+password service; physical authenticator/browser testing is separate.
